WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.713 --> 00:00:21.528
"Whew! It sure is hot today," Henry's friend Cole said.

2
00:00:21.548 --> 00:00:25.091
"That's why we're getting ice cream, remember?"

3
00:00:25.912 --> 00:00:27.694
Henry pointed to a shop just ahead.

4
00:00:28.614 --> 00:00:30.136
It was called the Sweet Shop.

5
00:00:31.196 --> 00:00:34.677
A board on the sidewalk outside listed the store's special flavors.

6
00:00:35.617 --> 00:00:41.459
"Today's special flavors are raspberry mint chip and bubble gum banana swirl," Cole read aloud.

7
00:00:41.479 --> 00:00:44.920
"Maybe I'll try bubble gum banana swirl.

8
00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.281
No Wait, I think I'll get marshmallow fudge.

9
00:00:48.541 --> 00:00:49.381
That's my favorite."

10
00:00:51.342 --> 00:00:55.183
A bell over the door jingled when Henry and Cole entered the ice-cream shop.

11
00:00:56.943 --> 00:00:58.564
Several people were waiting in line.

12
00:00:59.424 --> 00:01:02.186
The woman behind the counter looked up when she heard the bell.

13
00:01:02.206 --> 00:01:04.909
"Hello, boys," she said.

14
00:01:04.929 --> 00:01:06.670
"I'll be with you shortly."

15
00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:08.552
"Thanks, Mrs.

16
00:01:08.632 --> 00:01:09.833
Sweet," Henry said.

17
00:01:10.853 --> 00:01:12.455
Everyone in Belltown liked Mrs.

18
00:01:12.515 --> 00:01:14.336
Sweet and her homemade ice cream.

19
00:01:15.377 --> 00:01:18.179
She had owned the Sweet Shop since Henry's parents were babies.

20
00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:22.102
The shop never changed much, but the flavors did.

21
00:01:22.803 --> 00:01:24.925
Mrs. Sweet was always inventing new ones.

22
00:01:25.946 --> 00:01:28.648
Henry and Cole waited until it was their turn to be served.

23
00:01:29.904 --> 00:01:34.765
"I'll try one scoop of raspberry mint chip in a cone, please," Henry said.

24
00:01:34.785 --> 00:01:37.986
"Marshmallow fudge for me," Cole said.

25
00:01:38.006 --> 00:01:40.487
"Coming right up, boys."

26
00:01:43.128 --> 00:01:47.069
Mrs. Sweet picked up two cones and leaned into the cooler to get the ice cream.

27
00:01:47.989 --> 00:01:48.929
Henry looked around.

28
00:01:48.949 --> 00:01:51.290
"This place is busy today."

29
00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:53.710
"It sure is.

30
00:01:54.671 --> 00:01:58.152
Hot weather always makes people want a nice cool treat!"

31
00:01:58.452 --> 00:01:59.412
Mrs. Sweet winked.

32
00:02:00.936 --> 00:02:02.537
"But you must know that already.

33
00:02:02.557 --> 00:02:05.179
How's business at your lemonade stand?"

34
00:02:05.199 --> 00:02:07.521
"Great," Henry said.

35
00:02:07.541 --> 00:02:12.145
"That reminds me, we promised to bring back some ice cream for Maggie."

36
00:02:13.165 --> 00:02:13.926
Cole nodded.

37
00:02:13.946 --> 00:02:16.888
"She wants a scoop of cherry vanilla in a cup."

38
00:02:20.911 --> 00:02:23.893
Soon Henry and Cole were back outside with their ice cream.

39
00:02:23.913 --> 00:02:26.816
"We'd better hurry," Henry said.

40
00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:31.190
"We promised Maggie we'd be back soon to help with the customers."

41
00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:36.594
"Yeah." Cole licked his ice cream, which was already starting to melt in the heat.

42
00:02:36.614 --> 00:02:42.598
"Besides," he added, "Maggie will be mad if her ice cream melts before we get back."

43
00:02:46.401 --> 00:02:50.904
Half a dozen people were clustered around the lemonade stand when Henry and Cole reached it.

44
00:02:51.925 --> 00:02:53.506
Maggie saw the two boys coming.

45
00:02:53.526 --> 00:02:55.567
"Hurry up, you two!"

46
00:02:55.767 --> 00:02:56.288
she called.

47
00:02:57.104 --> 00:02:58.986
"I can't do everything by myself!"

48
00:02:59.006 --> 00:03:01.908
"Sorry. We tried to hurry."

49
00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:04.830
Henry ate the last bite of his ice-cream cone.

50
00:03:05.731 --> 00:03:09.154
Then he handed Maggie her ice cream and grabbed a pitcher of lemonade.

51
00:03:09.174 --> 00:03:11.376
"Who's next?"

52
00:03:11.696 --> 00:03:12.837
he called to the customers.

53
00:03:12.857 --> 00:03:16.119
"I am," a familiar voice said.

54
00:03:16.139 --> 00:03:20.123
"Dad!" Henry looked up and saw his father grinning at him.

55
00:03:20.143 --> 00:03:22.565
"What are you doing here?"

56
00:03:22.585 --> 00:03:26.608
"Are you writing a story about our lemonade stand, Uncle Kevin?"

57
00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:27.601
Maggie joked.

58
00:03:29.202 --> 00:03:30.323
Henry's father chuckled.

59
00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:33.025
He was a reporter for the local newspaper.

60
00:03:33.045 --> 00:03:35.207
"Nope," he said.

61
00:03:35.227 --> 00:03:37.149
"I'm just here for lemonade."

62
00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:41.212
As Henry handed his father a cup, an older man arrived.

63
00:03:41.232 --> 00:03:44.735
"Well, hello, Kevin," he greeted Henry's father.

64
00:03:44.756 --> 00:03:46.817
"Mr. Moss!"

65
00:03:47.158 --> 00:03:48.359
Henry's dad smiled.

66
00:03:48.379 --> 00:03:50.781
"I've been meaning to call you.

67
00:03:51.161 --> 00:03:54.364
You did a great job fixing our garage door last weekend."

68
00:03:55.856 --> 00:03:57.717
"One lemonade, please," Mr.

69
00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:59.858
Moss said to Henry, handing him a quarter.

70
00:04:01.018 --> 00:04:02.759
Then he turned back to Henry's father.

71
00:04:02.779 --> 00:04:06.341
"I'm glad you're pleased with the repair job," he said.

72
00:04:06.361 --> 00:04:10.102
"Speaking of garages, did you hear about Mr.

73
00:04:10.182 --> 00:04:11.263
O'Malley's new car?"

74
00:04:13.304 --> 00:04:16.265
The two men wandered away with their lemonade, still chatting.

75
00:04:16.285 --> 00:04:19.306
"Mr. Moss fixed your garage door?"

76
00:04:19.667 --> 00:04:20.707
Cole asked Henry.

77
00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:22.748
"I thought he was an art teacher."

78
00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:26.141
"He retired last year," Maggie told him.

79
00:04:26.161 --> 00:04:28.963
"Now he does odd jobs around town.

80
00:04:29.903 --> 00:04:34.206
My parents hired him to paint our garden shed, and they said he did a great job."

81
00:04:34.926 --> 00:04:35.486
She grinned.

82
00:04:35.506 --> 00:04:39.729
"Except he likes to chatter while he works about things going on around town."

83
00:04:39.749 --> 00:04:44.151
"Mr. Moss loves to gossip," Henry agreed.

84
00:04:45.211 --> 00:04:46.152
Cole looked around.

85
00:04:46.172 --> 00:04:48.193
"Whew!" he said.

86
00:04:48.213 --> 00:04:51.035
"That's the last of our customers for right now."

87
00:04:51.055 --> 00:04:53.356
"Yeah," Maggie said.

88
00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.742
"The lemonade stand has been really busy all day."

89
00:04:57.723 --> 00:04:58.683
She glared at the boys.

90
00:04:58.703 --> 00:05:02.146
"Especially while you two were gone."

91
00:05:03.527 --> 00:05:04.247
Henry grinned.

92
00:05:04.267 --> 00:05:06.989
"Having more customers means we make more money."

93
00:05:07.009 --> 00:05:08.530
"That's true."

94
00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:09.831
Maggie looked happier.

95
00:05:09.851 --> 00:05:12.153
"I need all the money I can get.

96
00:05:13.073 --> 00:05:15.915
I'm still saving up to enter the horse show at my barn.

97
00:05:16.836 --> 00:05:19.838
And we're not making much from our detective business these days."

98
00:05:19.858 --> 00:05:22.280
"True." Henry nodded.

99
00:05:23.144 --> 00:05:25.365
"We haven't had a new case in a few days."

100
00:05:26.806 --> 00:05:28.507
Cole helped himself to some lemonade.

101
00:05:28.527 --> 00:05:29.928
"You're right.

102
00:05:30.448 --> 00:05:32.790
Maybe we've solved all the mysteries in Belltown!"

103
00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.291
"Maybe," Henry said.

104
00:05:36.412 --> 00:05:37.392
Maggie looked worried.

105
00:05:37.412 --> 00:05:38.293
"I hope not.

106
00:05:38.793 --> 00:05:40.734
Entering that horse show is expensive."

107
00:05:40.754 --> 00:05:42.795
"Here comes another customer."

108
00:05:43.576 --> 00:05:44.876
Cole pointed down the street.

109
00:05:46.297 --> 00:05:46.837
"Who is it?"

110
00:05:47.618 --> 00:05:51.160
When Henry turned to look, he saw a young man he didn't recognize.

111
00:05:52.232 --> 00:05:53.913
A moment later the man reached them.

112
00:05:54.614 --> 00:05:56.275
But he didn't even glance at the lemonade.

113
00:05:56.295 --> 00:05:58.716
"Are you the kid detectives I've heard about?"

114
00:05:59.096 --> 00:05:59.737
he demanded.

115
00:05:59.757 --> 00:06:05.000
"Because I need someone to help me prove something—my ice-cream flavor was stolen!"
